{
 "label": "daily-pattern-line-filter-loki-defaults",
 "date": "2026-11-16",
 "set": "pattern-line-filter",
 "description": "Pattern line filters (PR for semantics/pattern-line-filter): an empty pattern matches only the empty line (Loki pkg/logql/log/pattern), so `|> \"\"` keeps no line and `!> \"\"` keeps every one; the proxy translated it to match-all. P1 and P2 are log queries over the api-gateway streams, P3 is a count_over_time over a pattern that matches no nginx line and P4 over a pattern that matches every GET request line (the access log has the method after an opening quote). Run with the control set.",
